  <Document>
    <name>💨 LIVE WIND</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<h2>LIVE WIND — BEAUFORT SCALE</h2><p><b>Data time:</b> 2026-09-21 13:00 UTC<br/><b>Source updated:</b> Mon, 21 Sep 2026 13:27:44 GMT<br/><b>Processed:</b> 2026-09-21 22:08 UTC<br/><b>Status:</b> LIVE / CURRENT MODEL (analysis)</p><p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/wind/legend.png?v=2026-09-21_2208_UTC" width="600" alt="legend"><br>WIND — BEAUFORT SCALE (colors follow force, dark purple = Force 12 only):<br/><b>F0</b> — Calm (0–0.99 kt)<br/><b>F1</b> — Light air (1–3 kt)<br/><b>F2</b> — Light breeze (4–6 kt)<br/><b>F3</b> — Gentle breeze (7–10 kt)<br/><b>F4</b> — Moderate breeze (11–16 kt)<br/><b>F5</b> — Fresh breeze (17–21 kt)<br/><b>F6</b> — Strong breeze (22–27 kt)<br/><b>F7</b> — High wind (28–33 kt)<br/><b>F8</b> — Gale (34–40 kt)<br/><b>F9</b> — Strong gale (41–47 kt)<br/><b>F10</b> — Storm (48–55 kt)<br/><b>F11</b> — Violent storm (56–63 kt)<br/><b>F12</b> — Hurricane-force (≥64 kt)<br/>Maximum this run: <b>25 kt</b> (Beaufort 6). Arrows point where the air moves.</p><p><b>Source:</b> NOAA/NCEP Great Lakes Wave Unstructured v2.1 (GLWUv2.1, WAVEWATCH III) — UGRD/VGRD surface analysis<br/><a href="https://nomads.ncep.noaa.gov/pub/data/nccf/com/glwu/prod/glwu.20260921/glwu.grlc_2p5km.t13z.grib2">https://nomads.ncep.noaa.gov/pub/data/nccf/com/glwu/prod/glwu.20260921/glwu.grlc_2p5km.t13z.grib2</a></p><p>Transparent outside valid water data so existing project layers (shipwrecks, lighthouses, harbors, parks) stay visible. Turn on/off independently of the ice, wave and temperature layers.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
